transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "571ee7e4f8997fdfae74f800edd84d0efce760607b5043aa85a8d9d81962095f" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/format-audit/database-repair/verification.json" "basis" 653} {"question" "q-336441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=4{t}^{3}-{t}^{2},$ where $t$ is measured in seconds. Find the time when the particle's acceleration is equal to $a=70\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nThe acceleration is $70\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ at\n$t=$\n{{field-1}} seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "0746d23ff8748e14caba650c7122bb780dd7c051a19a0ecd3d0b1e6890a59502" "basis" 778 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =12{t}^{2}-2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(12{t}^{2}-2t) \\\\  & =24t-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=70,$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}70 & =24t-2 \\\\ 24t & =72 \\\\ t & =3\\text{ }\\text{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration is $70\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ at $t=3$ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "0746d23ff8748e14caba650c7122bb780dd7c051a19a0ecd3d0b1e6890a59502" "basis" 778 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a473f950ca02cb6db7ee132f1b9de240125d4e28540344c2d876322ff93788c7" "basis" 778 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336441" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "0746d23ff8748e14caba650c7122bb780dd7c051a19a0ecd3d0b1e6890a59502" "basis" 778 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336441" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "0746d23ff8748e14caba650c7122bb780dd7c051a19a0ecd3d0b1e6890a59502" "basis" 778 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-215" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity $v$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $v(t) = -6t-3t^2$. Calculate the acceleration of the particle at time $t$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/example-215.json" "file_sha256" "71b1e773a337012c787a32bdd1bcb66a9a53590aa6d7cb3e9c1d8ab327fa3677" "basis" 778 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-215" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-6t-3{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =-6-6t \\\\  & =-6(1+t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/example-215.json" "file_sha256" "71b1e773a337012c787a32bdd1bcb66a9a53590aa6d7cb3e9c1d8ab327fa3677" "basis" 778 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-216" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position $x$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $x(t) = 1+2t+3t^2+4t^3$. Calculate the acceleration of the particle at time $t=0$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/example-216.json" "file_sha256" "92b8ee01c1b36adfbee1b633cbc7fb04a1672a2f309cc1db700837ff6497897e" "basis" 778 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-216" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $x(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+2t+3{t}^{2}+4{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =2+6t+12{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2+6t+12{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =6+24t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=0$, we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(0) & =6+24(0) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration when $t=0$ is $6$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/example-216.json" "file_sha256" "92b8ee01c1b36adfbee1b633cbc7fb04a1672a2f309cc1db700837ff6497897e" "basis" 778 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-2360" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity $v$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of a particle at time $t$ (in seconds) is given by $v(t)=3{t}^{2}-24t+45.$ Calculate the velocity of the particle when the acceleration $a$ is equal to $0\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-2360" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-24t+45) \\\\  & =6t-24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=0,$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =6t-24 \\\\ 6t & =24 \\\\ t & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, to calculate the velocity at time $t=4,$ we substitute this into the equation for the velocity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(4) & =3(4)^{2}-24(4)+45 \\\\  & =48-96+45 \\\\  & =-3\\text{ m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity when $a=0\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ is $-3\\,\\text{m/s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-2360" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file