locity $v$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of a particle at time $t$ (in seconds) is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)+1.$ Calculate the velocity of the particle when the acceleration $a$ is equal to $\\frac{1}{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nWhen $a=\\frac{1}{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2},$ the velocity is $v=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m/s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-336435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=\\frac{1}{2},$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{1}{t+1} \\\\ t+1 & =2 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, to calculate the velocity at time $t=1,$ we substitute this into the equation for the velocity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+1)+1 \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+1)\\text{ m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity when $a=\\frac{1}{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ is $v=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+1\\,\\text{m/s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-336435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe66d890c0d20832f8197c4aff0809c957f75deffbbfe81604a7b8ed13ae9c7b"} {"question" "q-336435" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-336435" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(2)+1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-315535" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity $v$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of a particle at time $t$ is given by $v(t)={t}^{3}{e}^{3t-3},$ where $t$ is measured in seconds. Calculate the acceleration of the particle at $t=1$ second.\n\n$a(1)=$\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-315535" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}{e}^{3t-3}) \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}{e}^{3t-3}+3{t}^{3}{e}^{3t-3} \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}(1+t){e}^{3t-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration when $t=1$ second, we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =3(1)^{2}(1+1){e}^{3(1)-3} \\\\  & =3(1)(2){e}^{0} \\\\  & =6\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-315535" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe66d890c0d20832f8197c4aff0809c957f75deffbbfe81604a7b8ed13ae9c7b"} {"question" "q-315535" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-315535" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-2358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=6{t}^{3}-19{t}^{2}+13,$ where $t$ is measured in seconds. Find the time when the particle's acceleration is equal to $a=70\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-2358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{3}-19{t}^{2}+13) \\\\  & =18{t}^{2}-38t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(18{t}^{2}-38t) \\\\  & =36t-38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=70,$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}70 & =36t-38 \\\\ 36t & =108 \\\\ t & =3\\,\\text{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the time when the acceleration is $a=70\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ is $3$ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-2358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe66d890c0d20832f8197c4aff0809c957f75deffbbfe81604a7b8ed13ae9c7b"} {"question" "q-2358" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-2358" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$2$ seconds"] ["text" "$3$ seconds"] ["text" "$3.5$ seconds"] ["text" "$4.5$ seconds"] ["text" "$5$ seconds"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-2358" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$3$ seconds"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-336455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The displacement $s$ of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)={t}^{2}+\\frac{6}{t+2}.$ Find the particle's acceleration at time $t.$\n\n$a(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-336455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+\\frac{6}{t+2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+6(t+2)^{-1}) \\\\  & =2t-6(t+2)^{-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-6(t+2)^{-2}) \\\\  & =2+12(t+2)^{-3} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{12}{(t+2)^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-336455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe66d890c0d20832f8197c4aff0809c957f75deffbbfe81604a7b8ed13ae9c7b"} {"question" "q-336455" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-336455" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{12}{(t+2)^3}+2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-336441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=4{t}^{3}-{t}^{2},$ where $t$ is measured in seconds. Find the time when the particle's acceleration is equal to $a=70\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nThe acceleration is $70\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ at\n$t=$\n{{field-1}} seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-336441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =12{t}^{2}-2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(12{t}^{2}-2t) \\\\  & =24t-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=70,$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}70 & =24t-2 \\\\ 24t & =72 \\\\ t & =3\\text{ }\\text{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration is $70\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ at $t=3$ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-336441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe66d890c0d20832f8197c4aff0809c957f75deffbbfe81604a7b8ed13ae9c7b"} {"question" "q-336441" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-336441" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-336444" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)={t}^{2}+4\\sqrt{t},$ where $t$ is measured in seconds. Find the particle's acceleration at $t=1$ second.\n\n$a(1)=$\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-336444" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+4\\sqrt{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+4{t}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =2t+2{t}^{-1/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t+2{t}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =2+2(-\\frac{1}{2}){t}^{-3/2} \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=1$ second, we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =2-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(1)^{3}}} \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-336444" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe66d890c0d20832f8197c4aff0809c957f75deffbbfe81604a7b8ed13ae9c7b"} {"question" "q-336444" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-336444" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-315674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=6{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2},$ where $t$ is measured in seconds. Find the time when the particle's acceleration is equal to $a=150\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nThe acceleration is $150\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ at\n$t=$\n{{field-1}} seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-315674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =18{t}^{2}+6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(18{t}^{2}+6t) \\\\  & =36t+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=150,$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}150 & =36t+6 \\\\ 36t & =144 \\\\ t & =4\\text{ }\\text{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration is $150\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ at $t=4$ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-315674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe66d890c0d20832f8197c4aff0809c957f75deffbbfe81604a7b8ed13ae9c7b"} {"question" "q-315674" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "q-315674" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/state.json" "file_sha256" "de533b3f0ea174bc67ccb1cadcf4de20f8d0fa65131bd93e4aba747cdd8130e1"} {"question" "e-215" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity $v$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $v(t) = -6t-3t^2$. Calculate the acceleration of the particle at time $t$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/example-215.json" "file_sha256" "71b1e773a337012c787a32bdd1bcb66a9a53590aa6d7cb3e9c1d8ab327fa3677"} {"question" "e-215" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-6t-3{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =-6-6t \\\\  & =-6(1+t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/example-215.json" "file_sha256" "71b1e773a337012c787a32bdd1bcb66a9a53590aa6d7cb3e9c1d8ab327fa3677"} {"question" "e-216" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position $x$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $x(t) = 1+2t+3t^2+4t^3$. Calculate the acceleration of the particle at time $t=0$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/example-216.json" "file_sha256" "92b8ee01c1b36adfbee1b633cbc7fb04a1672a2f309cc1db700837ff6497897e"} {"question" "e-216" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $x(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+2t+3{t}^{2}+4{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =2+6t+12{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2+6t+12{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =6+24t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=0$, we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(0) & =6+24(0) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration when $t=0$ is $6$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/example-216.json" "file_sha256" "92b8ee01c1b36adfbee1b633cbc7fb04a1672a2f309cc1db700837ff6497897e"} {"question" "q-2358" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$3$ seconds"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038045/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "1ba73689a61d1ef7674d89639cbcb0cec436dfdf9e7ddc3e73448a9266303bd3" "reviewer_session" "01a118ea-3923-70c2-acd9-0830602bde5f" "rationale" "Differentiating s(t)=6t^3−19t^2+13 twice gives a(t)=36t−38. Setting a(t)=70 yields 36t=108, hence t=3 seconds. Original option a (index 0) and the authentic worked solution agree. The captured submission was 5 seconds and was graded Incorrect; this review is a derived judgment, not a successful grade for 3 seconds. Preserve the authentic text choice and reconcile the stored math representation through the existing source-backed replacement path." "bindings" {"problem" "1e713454db94c1edf5b40de27448d23df192688bc8a87ed093bfe6924f46fe47" "worked_solution" "80502cc907a2f51f11ca38be25a870da211758c01c2669261f2f43aa57bff363" "original_field" "33b502d18cf6683463be76e66e65ee21b5e16b9df3d920246af234e1b1ec68b2" "reviewed_field" "1240446b9beb6cef24649b3be2b8b9fa73307658fe4638c3a92bd7350ac9266d" "raw_widget" "df3